  "derivation": {
    "suite": "Each scale emits scale repetitions; every repetition emits Alpha then Beta, and each fresh schema world emits 13 records: 6 linked-failure, 3 cleanup-before-spawn, and 4 abort-and-cleanup-after.",
    "dualScope": "main.bend calls Sc.scope twice per fresh world. Both tokens carry the same namespace/name; linked id 1 uses the first token and linked id 5 uses the second. Sc.assigned stores both members under the shared name, so cleanup observes [1,5].",
    "linked": "Six component spawns reserve ids 1..6; Parent edges are 2->1 and 4->2 and Link is 3->1. The failed registered cleanup rolls back only its staged cleanup command. The deferred barrier activates all six and relations. Successful cleanup traverses hierarchy 4,2,1, then member 5; the ordinary Link child 3 survives after unrelate. ComponentRemoved and Original streams are independently normalized to [1,2,4,5].",
    "before": "Cleanup is queued before scoped id 1 and plain id 2 in the same successful transaction. FIFO barrier order therefore sees an empty scope, then activates both; later cleanup removes only id 1.",
    "abort": "The seed reserves id 1. The failed scoped id 99 reserves id 2 and transaction rollback leaves that reservation consumed. The next successful scoped spawn therefore receives id 3; cleanup queued after it runs after activation and removes id 3, leaving id 1.",
